    "oai": {
      "build_dir": "builds/oai-zmq-release",
      "cmake": [
        "-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release",
        "-DOAI_ZMQ=ON",
        "-DENABLE_WERROR=OFF",
        "-DAUTO_DOWNLOAD_ASN1C=ON",
        "-DAVX512=OFF",
        "-DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=<root>/install/sysroot/usr"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH is required: find_library/find_path do not read CPATH or LIBRARY_PATH, so without it libsctp is reported missing even though the sysroot has it.",
        "libcap is optional -- CMakeLists.txt:688 guards its use with if(cap_FOUND), so the pkg-config warning is expected and harmless.",
        "AUTO_DOWNLOAD_ASN1C builds asn1c from source via autoreconf, which is why the autotools overlay and the relocation patches below exist.",
        "AVX512=OFF is required on this host, not a performance choice made lightly. Zen 4 defines __AVX512F__, so radio/zmq/zmq_simd.h takes its AVX-512 branch, and the only SIMDe in the Ubuntu noble archive is 0.7.2 which lacks simde_mm512_cvtepi16_epi32 / cvtepi32_ps / cvtps_epi32. OAI's own -DAVX512=OFF switches the build to -mno-avx512f -march=native and the branch compiles out. The alternative is vendoring a newer header-only SIMDe; revisit only if UE PHY throughput ever becomes the limit, which it is not at 23.04 MS/s over ZMQ."
      ],
      "source": "src/oai",
      "targets": [
        "nr-uesoftmodem",
        "oai_zmqdevif"
      ],
      "transitive_pins": [
